# S204's WITNESS, and the reason it needs one is worth stating: after
# W1.1 taught verify_rxt.py the corpus's other four line kinds, NO corpus
# line reaches its unknown-kind branch any more. Fixing the gap is what
# emptied the population of the row that guards it.
#
# All three parsers must REFUSE a kind they do not know rather than
# swallow it: leg A by name in its scope, run.sh through its catch-all
# hard error, verify_rxt.py by raising. A parser that treats a kind it
# does not know as a comment verifies nothing and says nothing, which is
# the quiet failure S204 plants.
#
# [DD-13b.W23.3] THE TOKEN MOVED, AND IT MOVED BECAUSE THE OLD ONE
# SHIPPED. This fixture used to carry `tag beta` and assert the
# NOT-IN-THIS-BUILD refusal, on the reasoning that a real later-wave
# keyword also proves "not in this build" and "unparseable" stay distinct
# answers. `tag` is a BLOCK production now, so that spelling asserts
# nothing — the fixture would be accepted by all three legs while the
# check named after it still reported a refusal it no longer gets.
# `no-such-kind` is chosen instead precisely because it is NOT a keyword
# and cannot become one: a hyphen-bearing token the format has never
# owned. The two answers stay distinguishable through a DIFFERENT pair —
# this file and `version_reserved.rxtin` — which is the general repair
# for a witness whose subject graduates: re-aim it at something that
# cannot graduate, and let a second fixture carry the tier it left.
pattern a+
no-such-kind beta
m "aaa" 0 3
